Third-party components
================================================================================

compVDO's own source is Apache-2.0. It depends on, but does not include, the
components below. Their licences apply to them, not to this project's code.

Desktop (Python)
----------------
PySide6 ................ LGPL v3 (or commercial), The Qt Company
    Imported at run time by the optional desktop GUI. The stdlib-only core and
    the command line do not use it. Note for anyone producing a *bundled*
    build (for example with PyInstaller): the LGPL requires that the user be
    able to replace the Qt libraries, which a single-file executable does not
    by itself satisfy.

Send2Trash ............. BSD 3-Clause (optional, Windows only)

FFmpeg / ffprobe ....... LGPL v2.1+ or GPL v2+, depending on the build
    Invoked as a separate external program over a pipe. It is not linked
    against, not bundled on Linux, and no FFmpeg source is included here.
    x265, used by the common GPL builds, is GPL v2+.

    If you distribute compVDO *together with* a GPL FFmpeg binary — the likely
    shape of a Windows package — the terms of that build apply to the combined
    distribution. Ship an LGPL build, or have users install FFmpeg themselves,
    if that is not what you want.

Android (Kotlin)
----------------
AndroidX, Jetpack Compose, Media3 ......... Apache-2.0, The Android Open
                                            Source Project
Kotlin and kotlinx.coroutines ............. Apache-2.0, JetBrains
Coil (coil-compose, coil-video) ........... Apache-2.0, Coil Contributors

